Title: Split corpus WP gate's pytest roots to avoid conftest collision
Created: 2026-09-28
Author: Codex

--- log ---
2026-09-28T16:00Z Codex created after REL ticket 1351 exposed the existing combined-root gate failure

--- body ---
## Context

`make check-corpus-wp` passes `tests/` and `libs/openalex-corpus/tests/` to a
single pytest invocation. Both roots define `conftest.py`, and collection can
import the library's `conftest` for repository tests. On padme at REL commit
`7cf4eee0`, the combined gate failed with missing `smoke_env` and
`run_compute` imports. The same `wp_corpus` selection passed when run once per
root: 1,380 repository tests and 25 library tests.

## Actions

1. Run the two roots in separate pytest invocations within the Makefile gate,
   preserving the marker and worker settings.
2. Test that a failure in either invocation fails the target; avoid silently
   skipping the library suite.
3. Verify the target on padme with corpus data available.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make check-corpus-wp` passes on padme with both suites selected.
- [ ] A failing root makes the target fail, with no false success from the
      other root.
- [ ] Required shared-infrastructure gates and independent review pass.
